DESCRIPTION:MICHAEL ST GEORGE + ROOTS N BLOOM Jamaican roots. Reggae. Dub. 
 Spoken word. Conscious music. The Presynct welcomes internationally acclai
 med Jamaican-born Michael St George for a special night of roots reggae\, 
 dub poetry\, rhythm and powerful storytelling. Born in Portland\, Jamaica 
 and raised in Kingston\, Michael St George is a poet\, singer\, songwriter
  and renowned dub performance artist whose music brings together roots reg
 gae\, spoken word\, world rhythms and jazz\, carrying messages of social j
 ustice\, connection\, universal love and positive change. With a career sp
 anning decades and continents\, Michael has performed and collaborated wit
 h artists across Jamaica\, Canada and Australia\, including OKA\, Dennis B
 ovell\, Earl “Chinna” Smith and Ollie McGill of The Cat Empire. In Aus
 tralia\, he has toured with OKA\, collaborated on their The Sunset Session
 s\, performed at the Sydney Opera House and was the closing act at GARMA 2
 017. Joining Michael are Sunshine Coast special guests ROOTS N BLOOM - a c
 ollective of women brought together through music\, culture and community.
  Their beautiful vocal harmonies\, global influences and heartfelt storyte
 lling create music centred around connection\, joy and belonging. Together
 \, Michael St George and Roots N Bloom make this a night built around regg
 ae\, roots\, soul and community - uplifting live music with something to s
 ay. Come early\, grab a drink and settle in for a night of conscious music
  and positive vibes. 📅 Saturday 3rd October ⏰ Doors 6:00pm (Happy Hou
 r) | Event Doors from 7:00pm 🎟 General $35+BF | Door $40 🔞 18+ Event
  🩴 NO Thongs Permitted 🚱 NO Outside Drink bottles
